WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.149 --> 00:00:08.230
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and they just
announced the main characters for the Spin

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:10.220
Off Show which turns out, is something of
a prequel.

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:12.509
Not in the way you expect, but I’ll explain
that too.

00:00:12.509 --> 00:00:17.869
Only 6 people were announced so it’s likely
they’ll continue to add people to the pilot

00:00:17.869 --> 00:00:19.400
before they shoot.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.820
The fact that they’re this far into the
process means there’s a chance that if they

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:28.689
can finish it by the time the regular show
comes back for break.

00:00:28.689 --> 00:00:33.510
The network can make a decision and put the
show into production for a fall 2015 debut

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:34.760
if they want.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:38.250
That doesn’t mean it will go down that way,
it just means if everything stays on track

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:42.930
and they shoot it in time, we might get to
watch it as early as Comic Con 2015.

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:46.140
I’ll talk more about that after I explain
the characters.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:56.120
And my weekly walking dead giveaway starts
now, all you have to do to enter is be a subscriber

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:57.300
and leave a comment.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:02.300
So there are 6 people total and all these
character descriptions are from Robert Kirkman’s

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:03.300
mouth.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:04.470
Number 1 is Sean Cabrera.

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:06.960
He’s A Latino male in his early 40s.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:10.740
He’s a good man trying to do right by everyone
in his life.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:14.250
I’m choosing to think of him as the Rick
of the Group for now.

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:18.750
Or maybe a cross between Rick and Shane, if
Shane hadn’t of gone completely nuts.

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:20.380
Number 2 is Cody Cabrera.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:23.600
Sean’s whip-smart and rebellious teenage
son.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:25.720
Known as the angriest kid in town.

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:30.480
I’m going to think of him as a younger version
of Daryl who’s got Glenn’s Brain.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:36.350
He has “Mischief Managed” written all
over him.

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:38.060
Number 3 is Nancy Tompkins.

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:41.600
She’s a thirtysomething single mom with
two kids.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:45.230
Nancy looks like the girl next door, but there’s
an edge to her.

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:50.240
I’m thinking of her as a cross between Andrea
if she had a child just because she was mid-30s

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:52.979
and a season 1 season 2 Carol.

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:57.380
Carol is about 10 years older than what Nancy’s
going to be, but she’s like the template

00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:59.210
Walking Dead Tiger Mom.

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:03.950
Nancy sounds like she’s going to be like
that, soft and caring like Andrea but capricious

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:08.360
enough that she’ll swing to Carol levels
of badassery when pushed.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:10.330
Number 4 is Nick Tompkins.

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:12.439
He’s Nancy’s screwed up teenage son.

00:02:12.439 --> 00:02:16.010
He’s too old to stay at home but too scared
to flee.

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:22.609
I’ll explain the flee part when I explain
the time period this all takes place.

00:02:22.609 --> 00:02:28.959
He kind of sounds like an early version of
Bob, screwed up teenager who’s too chicken

00:02:28.959 --> 00:02:36.069
to leave home has “Future Alcoholic” written
all over him.

00:02:36.069 --> 00:02:37.890
Number 5 is Ashley Tompkins.

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:41.349
She’s Nancy’s mostly-level headed teenage
daughter.

00:02:41.349 --> 00:02:49.349
Her ambition is in direct proportion to her
older brother’s failures.

00:02:49.349 --> 00:02:52.879
She loves her mom, but it’s time to get
out of Dodge.

00:02:52.879 --> 00:02:56.419
From the character description she sounds
exactly like what Beth is going to become

00:02:56.419 --> 00:02:57.790
in season 5.

00:02:57.790 --> 00:03:02.650
Or what she started to become at the end of
season 4.

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:04.590
Much more ambitious about her own life.

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:08.739
Beth got really pissed at Daryl for just accepting
their fate.

00:03:08.739 --> 00:03:10.620
She was a big call to action for him.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:15.120
And it sounds like this new Ashley person
will be that for this new group of people.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:19.700
The last one, Number 6 is Andrea Chapman.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:21.719
I know there was already an Andrea on the
main show.

00:03:21.719 --> 00:03:26.180
But Kirkman explained that they have no relation
to each other and using the same name isn’t

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:29.849
meant to be an easter egg or anything.

00:03:29.849 --> 00:03:35.099
She’s described as a somewhat wilted flower
child, who has retreated to the outskirts

00:03:35.099 --> 00:03:37.930
of the city to recover from a Horrible Marriage.

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:42.090
Actually reading her story she really does
kind of sound like Andrea if she had Carol’s

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:43.090
life, pre-Apocalypse.

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:47.469
There’s a lot we can say about this group.

00:03:47.469 --> 00:03:52.299
First, they’re two single parent families
one with a dad, one with a mom.

00:03:52.299 --> 00:03:54.249
You can make all the Brady Bunch jokes you
want.

00:03:54.249 --> 00:03:58.459
But it does seem like they’re making the
spin off a family based group.

00:03:58.459 --> 00:03:59.459
At least at the beginning.

00:03:59.459 --> 00:04:03.780
This is a big change from the main show that
threw a bunch of strangers together with a

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:05.640
few scattered families.

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:09.599
These people will be much more of a family
unit.

00:04:09.599 --> 00:04:14.809
I think the hope is that by starting these
characters out in a much more intimate situation.

00:04:14.809 --> 00:04:17.669
We the audience will connect with them faster.

00:04:17.669 --> 00:04:22.039
I do tend to feel closer to a bonded group
of characters.

00:04:22.039 --> 00:04:32.770
On 
the other end of that spectrum.

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:36.720
Rick just acknowledged Daryl as his brother.

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:45.819
It took them four years to really become a
family.

00:04:45.819 --> 00:04:59.700
The spin off is just speeding that up.

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:08.419
There’s also the fact that you have a teenage
girl and a teenage boy in the group, and two

00:05:08.419 --> 00:05:10.710
single women with one single adult man.

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:13.010
So you can start the ‘shipping right here.

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:16.580
I’ll be interested to see if they go straight
for a love triangle with the adults and romeo

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:17.580
juliet the teenagers.

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:19.430
Young Love in the age of apocalypse.

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:22.370
I guess that kind of makes it sound like the
X-Men sequel.

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:24.729
Which is just another badass movie I can’t
wait to see.

00:05:24.729 --> 00:05:31.629
Supposedly part of the reason they chose to
go with Older Teenagers was because of all

00:05:31.629 --> 00:05:35.449
the trouble they had shooting with Chandler
Riggs when he was younger.

00:05:35.449 --> 00:05:39.110
Child labor laws make it so that you only
get to shoot with kids for like half a normal

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:40.110
day.

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:41.110
If they’re really young.

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:47.470
Like Carl in Season 1, you can only shoot
with them for a few hours per day.

00:05:47.470 --> 00:05:54.610
Normal shoots can sometimes take up to 18
hours.

00:05:54.610 --> 00:05:58.230
None of the characters are from the comics
and there’s no word on where this would

00:05:58.230 --> 00:05:59.230
be set.

00:05:59.230 --> 00:06:00.330
Which city they’d be in.

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:04.099
Now next big question: I know you’re asking
when does this take place.

00:06:04.099 --> 00:06:08.180
It’s a prequel right?

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:11.319
It’s supposedly going to take place in the
early days of the outbreak.

00:06:11.319 --> 00:06:14.009
It will chronicle the attempts to contain
the virus.

00:06:14.009 --> 00:06:18.310
Of Course there will be massive groups of
walkers, but the popluation won’t be nearly

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:19.939
as decimated.

00:06:19.939 --> 00:06:24.669
Society won’t have been destroyed but walkers
will start popping up everywhere.

00:06:24.669 --> 00:06:28.320
So we’ll be seeing the world react to them
for the first time.

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:32.930
Robert Kirkman is doing most of the writing
with the help of his partner at Skybound,

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:34.189
Dave Erickson.

00:06:34.189 --> 00:06:37.530
Erickson will be the official showrunner.

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:40.819
Robert Kirkman is way too busy to run a show.

00:06:40.819 --> 00:06:45.280
And he still has to help write the main show
too.

00:06:45.280 --> 00:07:01.340
The whole thing will borrow a lot of 
the behind the scenes talent of the main show,

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:02.960
but the difference is, from a production standpoint.

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:05.189
Robert Kirkman’s Skybound company is in
charge.

00:07:05.189 --> 00:07:06.879
So he stands to make a lot more money from
this show than from the main show if it’s

00:07:06.879 --> 00:07:07.879
successful.

00:07:07.879 --> 00:07:11.460
Frank Darabont developed the main show originally
with Kirkman’s help.

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:16.120
At the time, Kirkman didn’t have the ability
to produce the show himself, so AMC did a

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:32.259
lot of the heavy lifting.

00:07:32.259 --> 00:07:41.159
Next big question, when can we watch it?

00:07:41.159 --> 00:07:43.199
As I said earlier, they’re casting now.

00:07:43.199 --> 00:07:46.439
So if they can finish the pilot by the spring
next year.

00:07:46.439 --> 00:07:50.680
Unless there’s some huge catastrophe, AMC
can order it to series and they can shoot

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:56.610
episodes for a Fall 2015 release.

00:07:56.610 --> 00:08:07.479
That’s if they 
decide to air the series alongside the main

00:08:07.479 --> 00:08:08.479
show.

00:08:08.479 --> 00:08:16.639
They could always choose to air it during
another part of the year.

00:08:16.639 --> 00:08:42.570
And there’s been no word on how many episodes
per season they’re envisioning.

00:08:42.570 --> 00:08:55.760
It’s just a pilot right now, so we probably
won’t know more till they air that pilot.

00:08:55.760 --> 00:09:01.440
If you can make it to San Diego Comic Con
next summer, there’s a 99 percent chance

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:10.670
they’ll screen the pilot there.

00:09:10.670 --> 00:09:12.410
Unless something really horrible goes wrong.

00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:16.200
It will be canon with the main series.

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:23.970
I 
think it’s around 2009-2010 where we are

00:09:23.970 --> 00:09:24.970
right now.

00:09:24.970 --> 00:09:28.700
Kirkman said he’d never reveal the specific
year the outbreak started, other than it was

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:38.410
within a couple years of the start of the
comics.

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:40.030
Which was about 2003-2004.

00:09:40.030 --> 00:09:43.720
I guess you could say the spin off will take
place around 2-3 years before season 1 of

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:44.720
the main show.

00:09:44.720 --> 00:09:49.150
Let me know what you think about the characters
they announced and what kind of a villain

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:51.200
do you think we’ll see?

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:56.310
I know it’s not going to be comic book characters,
but that doesn’t mean Kirkman won’t borrow

00:09:56.310 --> 00:10:03.800
a villain from the comics and give them a
different name on the show.

00:10:03.800 --> 00:10:06.130
We only have about two more weeks before it
comes back.

00:10:06.130 --> 00:10:07.410
October 12th.

